'''Cut Content''' refers to entities, mechanics, objects, graphics, etc. that didn't make it into the final game but are still present within the game's data.

== Cut Vanilla Content ==
=== Pressure Plates ===
[[file:PressurePlates.png|120px]]

Pressure plates can be found in the game files and could have served as another type of [[obstacle]]. They are fully functional and can do the following things:
* Nothing
* Spawn a random chest
* Spawn 6 Attack Flies
* Spawn 6 Troll Bombs
* Activate Curse of Darkness for the rest of the floor
* Spawn a random pickup
* Spawn 15 random coins

{{dlc|a}} Buttons appear in rooms.

=== Various Half Hearts ===
[[file:SoulHalves.png|70px]]

Half [[Soul Heart]] and [[Black Heart]] pickups are in the game files, but they cannot be found in-game.

{{dlc|a+}} [[Half Soul Heart]]s are an unlockable pickup.

=== Colored Destructibles ===
[[file:ColoredDestructibles.png|400px]]

There are several colored versions of certain destructibles, which could have served a purpose similar to [[tinted rock]]s.

{{dlc+|r}} [[Marked Skull]]s are an unlockable obstacle through {{a|A Secret Exit}}.{{dlc-}}

=== Sisters Vis ===
[[file:SistersVisUnlock.png]]

A boss version of the [[Vis]] enemy that could have appeared in {{s|Sheol}}. According to the unused corresponding achievement file, Sisters Vis would have been unlocked by beating Sheol 10 times. The Sisters Vis were also a boss in ''Gish'', one of Edmund McMillen's previous games.
* {{dlc+|a+}} [[Sisters Vis|This boss]] can be encountered, but can appear in all environments of [[Chapter 3]], {{dlc|nr}} all environments of [[chapter 4]] and requires unlocking {{a|Something wicked this way comes+!}}.{{dlc-}}

=== Unused 12 Room Charge ===
[[file:BOIRebirth12Charge.png|20px]]

By editing the game's "items.xml" file and setting an item to ''maxcharges=12'', it's possible to see the charge bar in-game.
* {{dlc+|a}} The bar is used for the {{i|Mega Blast}} item, which has a 12-room charge.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|a+}} The bar is also used for the {{i|Delirious}} and {{i|Eden's Soul}} items, which have 12-room charges.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} The bar is also used for {{i|Alabaster Box}}, {{i|Larynx}}, {{i|Jar of Wisps}}, {{i|Everything Jar}}, {{i|Mega Mush}}, and for various consumables for {{i|Blank Card}}, {{i|Placebo}}, and {{i|Clear Rune}}.{{dlc-}}

